IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g2-readings`
IMPORT `g2-art3-4-commissioner`
IMPORT `g2-art5-charity-test`
IMPORT `g2-art6-purposes`
IMPORT `g2-art7-public-benefit`
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`
IMPORT `ind-a-tests-fixtures`

-- ind-a-tests-art3-7.l4: independent tests of Articles 3 to 7 (the Commissioner, the charity test, charitable purposes, public benefit).
-- Expected values from WORK/ind-a/expectations.md (S4.x, S5.x, S6.x, S7.x). Discretions ("reasonable degree", "appears to", "considers") are supplied as stated inputs.

§ `ind-a tests: Articles 3 to 7`

§§ `Helpers`

`ind-a J` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`

-- Facts that Article 6(2) reads, none of them true or relevant.
`ind-a no 6(2) facts` MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING

GIVEN sick IS A BOOLEAN, regen IS A BOOLEAN, civic IS A BOOLEAN, sport IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, need IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, public IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, care IS A BOOLEAN, eq IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, dv IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
`ind-a 6(2) facts` sick regen civic sport need public care eq dv MEANS
    `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE
        `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
        `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS sick
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS regen
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS civic
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS sport
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS need
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS public
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS care
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS eq
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS dv

GIVEN p IS A Purpose
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`ind-a pf` p MEANS `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` WITH purpose IS p, facts IS `ind-a no 6(2) facts`

GIVEN p IS A Purpose
      f IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a charitable` p f MEANS `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-a J` p f

GIVEN d IS A STRING
      h IS A `Head of charitable purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a head is charitable` d h MEANS `ind-a charitable` (`ind-a purpose under` d h) `ind-a no 6(2) facts`

-- A determination of public benefit: who, what was found, and what was done.
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`, provides IS A BOOLEAN, intends IS A BOOLEAN, guidance IS A BOOLEAN, compared IS A BOOLEAN, sectionOnly IS A BOOLEAN, conditions IS A BOOLEAN, presumed IS A BOOLEAN, onlyIdentified IS A BOOLEAN, treatedIdentified IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`ind-a determination` who provides intends guidance compared sectionOnly conditions presumed onlyIdentified treatedIdentified MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS who
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS provides
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS intends
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS guidance
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS compared
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS sectionOnly
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS conditions
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS presumed
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS onlyIdentified
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS treatedIdentified

-- The Commissioner finds public benefit provided to a reasonable degree, having done all Article 5(5) and 7 require.
`ind-a sound finding of public benefit` MEANS `ind-a determination` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The Commissioner finds no public benefit to a reasonable degree.
`ind-a sound finding of no public benefit` MEANS `ind-a determination` `the Commissioner` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The Commissioner finds an intention only.
`ind-a sound finding of intention only` MEANS `ind-a determination` `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

`ind-a no permissions` MEANS `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS EMPTY

GIVEN what IS A `What a constitution expressly permits`
      who IS A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
      acting IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`ind-a constitution permitting` what who acting MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH
        `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS LIST (`Permission that a constitution expressly makes` WITH
                                                                        `what the constitution expressly permits` IS what
                                                                        `the person permitted` IS who
                                                                        `acting in that capacity` IS acting)

GIVEN st IS A `Standing on the register`
      ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
GIVETH AN Entity
`ind-a entity with purposes` st ps MEANS
    `ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey Limited" st (LIST `a company`) TRUE (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`) ps

-- The charity test, with each purpose carrying no 6(2) facts, on the favoured readings and the text of 2 October 2026.
GIVEN st IS A `Standing on the register`
      ps IS A LIST OF Purpose
      cf IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      det IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a meets the charity test` st ps cf det order MEANS
    `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` `ind-a J` (`ind-a entity with purposes` st ps) (map `ind-a pf` ps) cf `the Chief Minister` det order

`ind-a two charitable purposes` MEANS LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`, `ind-a education purpose`
`ind-a g` MEANS `entered in the general section`

§§ `Article 4 (S4.2-01 to S4.3-03)`

-- S4.2-01 an act calculated to facilitate a function, not acting as a governor -> power (src:132)
#ASSERT `Art 4(2) the Commissioner has power to do the thing` TRUE FALSE
-- S4.2-02, S4.2-03 acting as a governor of a charity or of an entity with charitable purposes -> no power (src:132)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(2) the Commissioner has power to do the thing` TRUE TRUE
-- S4.2-04 an act not calculated to facilitate, conducive or incidental to any function -> no power (src:132)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 4(2) the Commissioner has power to do the thing` FALSE FALSE
-- S4.3-01 to S4.3-03 the three listed examples, each conducive to a function and not acting as a governor -> may (src:134-136)
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `ind-a J` `providing information to the public about the system of registration of charities` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `ind-a J` `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `ind-a J` `assisting an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions` TRUE FALSE

§§ `Article 5(1) (S5.1-01 to S5.1-10)`

-- S5.1-01 all purposes charitable, public benefit to a reasonable degree, no 5(2) clause -> meets (src:145-149)
#ASSERT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.1-02 a charitable purpose plus a purely ancillary trading purpose -> meets (src:148)
#ASSERT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` (LIST `ind-a education purpose`, `ind-a ancillary trading purpose`) `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.1-03 a non-charitable, non-ancillary purpose -> fails (src:146)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` (LIST `ind-a education purpose`, `ind-a private business purpose`) `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.1-04 ancillary purposes only -> fails (src:148)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` (LIST `ind-a ancillary trading purpose`) `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.1-05 no purposes at all -> fails (AMBIG-5, my reading)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` EMPTY `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.1-05 the other reading (vacuous truth) makes 5(1)(a) true for no purposes
#ASSERT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` (`ind-a entity with purposes` `ind-a g` EMPTY) EMPTY
-- S5.1-06 a registered charity (not an applicant) that only intends to provide public benefit -> fails (src:149)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of intention only` FALSE
-- S5.1-07 an applicant that intends to provide public benefit -> meets (src:149)
#ASSERT `ind-a meets the charity test` `an applicant for registration` `ind-a two charitable purposes` `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of intention only` FALSE
-- S5.1-09 public benefit not to a reasonable degree -> fails (src:149)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of no public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.1-10 a political party purpose put forward as ancillary -> fails (src:201)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` (LIST `ind-a education purpose`, `ind-a political party purpose`) `ind-a no permissions` `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE

§§ `Article 5(2) and (3) (S5.2-01 to S5.3-02)`

-- S5.2-01 the Minister for Health, acting as a Minister, may direct activities -> fails (src:150-151)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` (`ind-a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` NOTHING) TRUE) `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.2-01 AMBIG-4, the other reading ("a Minister" = Article 1's "the Minister", the Chief Minister today): the Minister for Health is not caught by (a)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.3 read as B` `the Chief Minister` (`ind-a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` NOTHING) TRUE)
-- and on that reading the Chief Minister, acting as such, is caught
#ASSERT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.3 read as B` `the Chief Minister` (`ind-a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)) TRUE)
-- S5.2-02 a governor may be a States member acting as such -> fails (src:152)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` (`ind-a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.2-03 a UK Secretary of State acting as such may control -> fails (src:153)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` (`ind-a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` `any equivalent of a Minister or of a member of the States Assembly in another jurisdiction` TRUE) `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.2-04 a States member serving in a private capacity -> passes 5(2) (src:150, src:154)
#ASSERT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` (`ind-a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` FALSE) `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.2-05 constitution silent -> passes 5(2) (src:150)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` `ind-a J` `the Chief Minister` `ind-a no permissions`
-- S5.2-06 fails 5(1) and has a 5(2) clause -> fails
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` (LIST `ind-a private business purpose`) (`ind-a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE
-- S5.3-01 a 5(2) clause and an Order under 5(3) for this entity -> meets, and meets only by virtue of the Order (src:155, src:233)
#ASSERT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` (`ind-a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 5(3) the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` `ind-a J` (`ind-a entity with purposes` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes`) (map `ind-a pf` `ind-a two charitable purposes`) (`ind-a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `the Chief Minister` `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` TRUE
-- S5.3-02 no Order specifies this entity or a description it is within -> fails
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a meets the charity test` `ind-a g` `ind-a two charitable purposes` (`ind-a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-a sound finding of public benefit` FALSE

§§ `Article 5(4) to (8) (S5.4-01 to S5.8-01)`

-- S5.4-01 the Commissioner must publish and maintain charity-test guidance; doing so discharges it
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 5(4) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on the charity test` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`publish and maintain guidance` `the Commissioner` `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`) AT 1
-- S5.5-01 any person determining the charity test must have regard (src:157)
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `any person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- S5.5-01 the Commissioner, the tribunal, a registered charity and a governor of a registered charity, in other relevant functions
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the Charity Tribunal` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `a registered charity` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `a governor` FALSE TRUE TRUE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- S5.5-01 the court is not named for "any other of their functions"
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the court` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- S5.6-01 consulted representatives, the Minister and others -> 5(6)(a) satisfied (src:159-162)
#ASSERT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- S5.6-01 consultation, then report, then issue -> in the order 5(6) requires
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `ind-a J` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 1 10)) (JUST (YMD 2025 2 1))
-- S5.6-02 the Minister not consulted -> breach of 5(6)(a)(ii) (src:161)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- S5.6-03 representatives appear to the Commissioner but were not consulted -> breach of 5(6)(a)(i) (src:160)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- S5.6-04 no report published -> breach of 5(6)(b) (src:163)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `ind-a J` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 1 10)) NOTHING
-- S5.6-06 the Minister to be consulted on 2025-06-01 is the Minister for External Relations; on 2026-10-27 the Chief Minister
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` (YMD 2025 6 1) `the favoured interpretation`) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` (YMD 2026 10 27) `the favoured interpretation`) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
-- S5.7-01 a copy provided within a reasonable time (input) -> in time; not provided -> breach (src:164)
#ASSERT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `ind-a J` (YMD 2025 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 3 20)) TRUE 0
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `ind-a J` (YMD 2025 3 1) NOTHING TRUE 0
-- S5.8-01 laid as soon as practicable (input) -> in time; not laid -> not (src:165)
#ASSERT `Art 5(8) the Minister laid the guidance and the report before the States in time` `ind-a J` (YMD 2025 3 20) (JUST (YMD 2025 4 15)) TRUE 0
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(8) the Minister laid the guidance and the report before the States in time` `ind-a J` (YMD 2025 3 20) NOTHING TRUE 0

§§ `Article 6 (S6.1-01 to S6.4-02)`

-- S6.1-01 to S6.1-15 one purpose under each head -> charitable (src:168-182)
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "food bank" `the prevention or relief of poverty`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "a school" `the advancement of education`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "a place of worship" `the advancement of religion`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "a hospice" `the advancement of health`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "a lifeboat service" `the saving of lives`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "community development" `the advancement of citizenship or community development`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "a heritage museum" `the advancement of the arts, heritage, culture or science`
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` (`ind-a purpose under` "public participation in football" `the advancement of public participation in sport`) (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` (`ind-a purpose under` "a recreation ground open to all" `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "human rights" `the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "racial harmony" `the promotion of religious or racial harmony`
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` (`ind-a purpose under` "equality and diversity" `the promotion of equality and diversity`) (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE))
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "environmental protection" `the advancement of environmental protection or improvement`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "relief of the elderly in need" `the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage`
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "an animal shelter" `the advancement of animal welfare`
-- S6.1-04 a vaccination campaign: prevention of disease, 6(2)(a) (src:185)
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` `ind-a private business purpose` (`ind-a 6(2) facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- S6.1-06 urban regeneration (6(2)(b)(i)); promoting volunteering (6(2)(b)(ii)) (src:187-188)
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` `ind-a private business purpose` (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` `ind-a private business purpose` (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- S6.1-14 a care home for elderly people in need, 6(2)(e) (src:193)
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` `ind-a private business purpose` (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- S6.1-16 a purpose the decider regards as analogous -> (p) (input)
#ASSERT `ind-a head is charitable` "an analogous purpose" `any other purpose that may reasonably be regarded as analogous to one of the above`
-- S6.2f-01 humanism -> charitable by 6(2)(f), under (p) and not (c) (src:194)
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` `ind-a humanism purpose` `ind-a no 6(2) facts`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `ind-a J` `ind-a humanism purpose`
-- S6.2c-01 chess / e-sports without physical exertion recorded under (h) -> not (h) (src:189)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a charitable` (`ind-a purpose under` "public participation in e-sports" `the advancement of public participation in sport`) (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- S6.2d-01 a facility only for fee-paying members of a private club -> not (i) (src:190-192)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a charitable` (`ind-a purpose under` "a members-only club" `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- S6.2d-02 open to all women of the public at large -> (i) (src:192)
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` (`ind-a purpose under` "a gym for women" `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- S6.2d-03 primarily for disabled persons -> (i) (src:191)
#ASSERT `ind-a charitable` (`ind-a purpose under` "a sensory garden" `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) (`ind-a 6(2) facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING)
-- S6.1-17 a private business purpose -> not charitable
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a charitable` `ind-a private business purpose` `ind-a no 6(2) facts`
-- S6.5-01, S6.5-02 advancing a party or promoting a candidate -> neither charitable nor ancillary (src:201)
#ASSERT `Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` `ind-a political party purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a charitable` `ind-a political party purpose` `ind-a no 6(2) facts`
-- S6.5-03 a purpose within (1)(b) on its face that advances a party -> 6(5) overrides (src:201)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a charitable` `ind-a party education purpose` `ind-a no 6(2) facts`

GIVEN adds1 IS A BOOLEAN, adds2 IS A BOOLEAN, explains IS A BOOLEAN, restricts IS A BOOLEAN, alters5 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)`
`ind-a regulations` adds1 adds2 explains restricts alters5 MEANS
    `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` WITH
        `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1)` IS adds1
        `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2)` IS adds2
        `the sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (2) make explanatory provision in relation to sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (1)` IS explains
        `amends or restricts the effect of any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f)` IS restricts
        `alters the effect of paragraph (5)` IS alters5

-- S6.3-01 adding a head on the Commissioner's recommendation -> valid (src:195-196)
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`ind-a regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S6.3-02 without the recommendation -> not authorised (src:195)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` FALSE (`ind-a regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S6.3-04 adding to (2) an explanation of an added head -> within; of an original head -> not (src:197, src:199)
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`ind-a regulations` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`ind-a regulations` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S6.4-01 restricting (1)(b) -> outside the power (src:199)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`ind-a regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- S6.4-02 altering 6(5) -> outside the power (src:200)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`ind-a regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Article 7 (S7.1-01 to S7.4-01)`

-- S7.1-01 7(2)-(3) bind the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court; not a governor or any person (src:203)
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the Commissioner` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the Charity Tribunal` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the court` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `a governor` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `any person` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- S7.2-01 the Commissioner had no regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a) -> the determination does not comply (src:204-208)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` (`ind-a determination` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
